e": 1,\n  "Questions": [\n    "Why did execution stop after one distinct candidate when the manuscript reports 49 remaining CPU executions? Was another resource limit reached, and can its host record be provided?",\n    "Can the remaining seven candidates be evaluated in the preregistered order and reported together with their actual validation MSEs and the resulting selection?",\n    "What precisely do the two CPU attempts represent, and what checks were performed by the reported independent verification?",\n    "Can the authors provide the fixed host implementation or an exact specification of feature scaling, intercept handling, penalty normalization, numerical solver, and software versions?",\n    "What scientific contribution beyond a routine baseline and a proposed search protocol should readers take from the completed work?",\n    "Can the authors supply response-scale context and, if host-authorized evidence is available, residual-level comparisons to make the eventual MSE differences interpretable? Independent evaluation would require a separate protocol."\n  ],\n  "Limitations": [\n    "The authors adequately acknowledge the absence of alternative measurements, statistical uncertainty estimates, test results, and evidence of global optimality.",\n    "The restricted candidate set and single fixed split limit conclusions even if the proposed experiment is completed. A winner would remain best among evaluated candidates on that split.",\n    "The unexplained early termination and missing implementation conventions should be stated more prominently as limitations of protocol completion and reproducibility.",\n    "No specific negative societal impact is evident from the described regression task. A brief statement about the dataset\'s provenance and intended use would make this assessment clearer; broader deployment claims would require application-specific evaluation."\n  ],\n  "Ethical Concerns": false,\n  "Soundness": 2,\n  "Presentation": 2,\n  "Contribution": 1,\n  "Overall": 3,\n  "Confidence": 4,\n  "Decision": "Reject"\n}\n```', True), 
